        "title": "What Big Data Sounds Like, The Hermeneutic Significance of the Arts for  Big Data in Digital Humanities",
        "description": "In recent scholarly past much attention has been called to the reductive nature of big data analysis regimes and to questions of the perceived but misleading neutral nature of large scale data and algorithms. This paper investigates a particular case of such issues and the frictional process of interfacing big data (analysis) and the hermeneutically geared humanities. We examine in particular the affordances produced by the re-introduction of the artist in a scientific environment.",
